                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "So I got this game free in the Curator program to review. I don't know the dev and a free game for me does not impact my decision in any manner whatsover. I buy 99% of the games I own and I own a lot of games.  In the end, I rate games based on their price and what they offer. This is a very close call for me because there is a good game here and it's very cheap, but the negatives outweigh the positives so I can't recommend the game.\n\nSo what's wrong with the game? First of all, the description is not accurate. Motion controllers don't really work. You're basically using the Touch controllers as a game pad. It's just a gaze and then press button mechanism. You could also use a pure gaze mechanism. I actually found the pure gaze mechanism to be better. Because pressing the button on my Touch controls seemed very unresponsive or lagged. I had to go slow and press the trigger button for it to register. It was very frustating selecting items.\n\nI can forgive the above, but I can't forgive the next problem. You can choose either a man or a woman Buried Alive. When I chose the male, I got stuck on a puzzle. It turns out, when I chose the female the next time, the papers that I had picked up earlier somehow all came together and showed a clue that is needed to progress. So I got stuck on a puzzle, simply because what should have happened, didn't for whatever reason. I can assure you that I took exactly the same steps and I was just lucky that my second time the clue actually popped up. So it seems there is a bug in gameplay that may prevent you from progressing, which is unfortunate in a puzzle game. Getting stuck for something that isn't your fault is a fatal error in a puzzle game.\n\nThe third thing that is wrong with the game is the ending. I will do it spoiler free but it's really a warning so I would recommend reading it. Here's the end spoiler: [spoiler] You warp forward about three times, then you get to a little girl ghost. She then proceeds to yell in your ear, twice. I guess it's a screaming jump scare. My ears hurt and it was not pleasant at all. Awful ending. [/spoiler]\n\nThe graphics weren't great. The UI and gameplay were clunky. I liked the puzzles. The puzzles were logical. I think the whole experience maybe is 10 minutes long. I got stuck the first time so I don't have the best estimate. But it's a very short puzzle escape room of 1 scenario. I would say it's worth .99 cents if it all was polished. But it's far from it. \n\nRate 4/10. Needs updates to be recommendable. Would be a really good game if the graphics and sounds were updated and if touch controllers were useable. Then I could easily recommend at .99 cents. Buried Alive should be a harrowing, immersive experience, not a clunky, frustrating experience.",
